2. Personal Data Processed by the App

Pipe Planner may process the following information:

email address, if the user creates or uses a user account
customer or contact information entered by the user
names and addresses of customers, work locations or projects
information relating to pipes, measurements, installations and work assignments
images that the user chooses to take or upload
text and descriptions entered by the user in the app

This information is provided by the user and is used to deliver the app’s features and functionality.

3. Purposes of Processing

The information may be processed in order to:

create and manage projects
record measurements, pipe routes and installations
document work assignments
store customer and project information
generate suggestions or analyses through OpenAI
ensure that the app functions as intended
respond to enquiries from users

We do not use personal data for targeted advertising, and we do not sell personal data.

4. Local Storage

Project information and other data entered by the user are primarily stored locally on the user’s device.

Locally stored data are normally not accessible to Almvik Brannvernservice AS unless the user actively sends the data to us or uses a feature that requires external processing.

The user is responsible for the customer information, images and project data entered into the app.

5. Use of OpenAI

Pipe Planner may provide features that use artificial intelligence through the OpenAI API.

When the user actively chooses to use such a feature, the following information may be sent to OpenAI:

images selected by the user for analysis
text or descriptions required to perform the analysis
relevant technical or project-related information entered by the user

The information is sent to OpenAI in order to process the request and generate a suggestion or analysis result. Information is not sent to OpenAI unless the user actively uses the relevant feature.

OpenAI acts as an external service provider for the artificial intelligence functionality. OpenAI states that content submitted through its API is not, by default, used to train or improve OpenAI’s models unless the API customer has expressly opted in to sharing data for that purpose.

Users should not submit images or text containing:

special categories of personal data
health information
national identification numbers
payment information
access codes or passwords
confidential information or unnecessary personal information

Artificial intelligence results may contain errors and should be reviewed by the user before being relied upon for technical or professional decisions.

6. Sharing of Personal Data

Personal data are shared only when necessary to:

provide a feature requested by the user
perform analysis through OpenAI
comply with legal obligations
protect the app, its users or the business against misuse and security incidents

We do not sell or rent personal data to third parties.

7. Camera and Images

Pipe Planner may request access to the camera or images stored on the user’s device.

This access is used only when the user chooses to:

take a photo within the app
select an existing image
attach an image to a project
send a selected image to OpenAI for analysis

The app does not need to access or transfer any images other than those specifically selected by the user.

8. Information Security

We use reasonable technical and organisational security measures to protect information against:

unauthorised access
loss or deletion
alteration
misuse
unlawful disclosure

Data transmitted between the app and external services are transferred using encrypted connections.

No digital storage or transmission method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

9. Retention and Deletion

Locally stored project information remains on the device until the user:

deletes the information within the app
resets the app’s data
uninstalls the app

Information required for a user account may be retained for as long as the account remains active or for as long as necessary to provide the service and comply with legal obligations.

Users may request access to, correction of or deletion of their personal data by contacting:

contact@almvikbrannvern.no

A request must contain sufficient information for us to identify the relevant account or personal data.

10. Children

Pipe Planner is a professional planning and work tool and is not designed or marketed specifically for children.

We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.

